From fc0ffd1fa9cc9ac0d9d6e72c85d5efa6391565ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 24bit192khz <118996408+24bit192kHz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:30:18 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 32/33] [local] ec/lenovo/mec1653: set the fan to automatic
 control in the bootblock

The EC powers up with the fan disengaged (full speed, unregulated) and
keeps it so until the host picks a mode. The vendor firmware sets
automatic early; coreboot never did, so the fan ran at full speed
through every boot and resume from S4 until Linux took over.
---
 src/ec/lenovo/mec1653/mec1653.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/mec1653/mec1653.c b/src/ec/lenovo/mec1653/mec1653.c
index 08682c0e38..933df0f215 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/mec1653/mec1653.c
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/mec1653/mec1653.c
@@ -18,6 +18,13 @@ void bootblock_ec_init(void)
 	ec_clear_out_queue();
 	ec_write(ec_read(0), 0x20);
 
+	// Fan to automatic control (HFSP 0x2f = 0x80, what thinkpad_acpi writes for
+	// "level auto"). The EC powers up with the fan disengaged - full speed,
+	// unregulated - and keeps it so until the host picks a mode; the vendor
+	// firmware sets it early. Without this the fan roared through every boot
+	// and every resume from S4 until Linux took over (seen 2026-11-02).
+	ec_write(0x2f, 0x80);
+
 	// Reset LEDs to power on state
 	// (Without this warm reboot leaves LEDs off)
 	ec_write(0x0c, 0x80);
